          "The architectural backbone of the Capstone Engine is structured around a closed-loop digital twin state machine that models physical material flows, information signals, and financial cost accruals across multi-tier networks. The engine continuously ingests upstream supplier telemetry, tracking shipment transit positions, port customs clearance delays, and component availability. Simultaneously, it interfaces with shop-floor manufacturing execution systems (MES), monitoring machine cycle velocities, tool wear sensor feeds, and queue accumulations at constrained workstations.",
          "By establishing a single, coherent mathematical model spanning procurement to customer delivery, the Capstone Engine enforces system-wide optimization invariants. Rather than allowing each tier to build redundant local buffers, the engine calculates global echelon inventory positions, placing safety stock where holding costs are lowest and pooling benefits are greatest. Concurrently, shop-floor job releases are dynamically gated by factory physics queue dampers, ensuring that manufacturing cells operate in the stable, high-velocity region of the utilization curve below the catastrophic asymptotic explosion threshold.",
